# Copy to .env.local (already gitignored) and adjust as needed.
#
# A physical device / Expo Go CANNOT reach "localhost" — that resolves to the phone itself,
# not your dev machine. Use your dev machine's LAN IPv4 address instead (same one Metro prints
# in the exp://192.168.x.x:8081 URL when you run `npx expo start`). Phone and PC must be on the
# same Wi-Fi network, and Windows Firewall may prompt to allow the Java process on port 8080 the
# first time you start the backend — allow it for Private networks.
#
# If you're only ever using an Android emulator (not a physical device), 10.0.2.2 also works
# and maps to the host machine's localhost.

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.0.108:8080
